title: Coalition Affairs
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; coalition_affairs_timer = 5
view-if: dvp_in_government and in_dvp_majority == 0 and coalition_dissent >= 1 and coalition_affairs_timer = 0
card-image: img/muller_cabinet.jpg
#subtitle: There is dissent within our coalition.

= Coalition Affairs

Our coalition is in trouble. [? if in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition: The left-leaning members of the <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span> and the <span style="color: #000000;">**Center**</span> ?][? if in_bourgeois_coalition: Members of the <span style="color: #000000;">**Center**</span> ?][? if in_center_right_coalition or in_hindenburg_coalition: The right-leaning members of the <span style="color: #000000;">**Center**</span> and the <span style="color: #3F7BC1;">**DNVP**</span> ?] are constantly criticizing us for our policies, and are threatening to call a vote of no confidence to collapse this government.

How do we reduce tensions with the coalition?

- @raise_spending: Agree to the <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span>'s plans to raise welfare spending.
- @cut_taxes: We will cut taxes to reduce dissent.
- @resources: Use our party resources to support our allies.
- @bring_down: Instead, we will bring down the government with a no-confidence vote, and call for new elections.
- @no_change: Take none of these actions.
- @easy_discard

@raise_spending
subtitle: -1 budget
view-if: in_weimar_coalition or in_grand_coalition
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough budget (need 1).
choose-if: budget > 0
on-arrival: budget -= 1; welfare += 1; workers_dvp += 3*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 5; unemployed_spd += 5; industrialist_dissent += 10; nationalist_dissent += 5; coalition_dissent = 0

Fine. By raising welfare spending, we have reduced dissent within the coalition.

@cut_taxes
subtitle: -2 budget
view-if: in_bourgeois_coalition or in_center_right_coalition or in_hindenburg_coalition
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough budget (need 2).
choose-if: budget > 1
on-arrival: budget -= 2; upper_tax_rates -= 1; new_middle_dvp += 4*(1-dissent); old_middle_dvp += 4*(1-dissent); spd_relation -= 3; unemployed -= 1 if unemployed >= 5; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if upper_tax_rates < 0; inflation += 0.6; economic_growth += 0.4; industrialist_dissent -= 10; labor_dissent += 3; coalition_dissent = 0

By cutting income taxes, we have reduced dissent within the coalition.

@resources
subtitle: -2 resources
view-if: historical_mode = 0
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources (need 2).
choose-if: resources >= 2
on-arrival: resources -= 2; coalition_dissent -= 1

By transferring campaign funds to our coalition partners, we can make our policies more acceptable to them. Some would call this corruption, but perhaps it is necessary to save democracy.

@no_change

No. We will not do this.

@bring_down
subtitle: Bring down this government before our opponents do.
on-arrival: dvp_in_government = 0; chancellor = "Brüning"; chancellor_party = "Z"; next_election_time = time + 3 if next_election_time > time+3; next_election_month = month + 3 if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year = year if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; dvp_toleration = 0; nationalist_strength += 8; pro_republic -= 5; workers_dvp -= 3; new_middle_dvp -= 3; rural_dvp -= 3; catholics_dvp -= 3; liberal_dissent += 5

We have called for a vote of no confidence in ourselves, and have brought down this government. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] currently rules as acting chancellor.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

